proof.text:
The direct diagonal construction is $\theta_{f,A}^{\mathrm{dir}}=\beta_A\delta_Aa_A^{-1}$; the prime-power orientation is $\theta_{f,R}=\beta_R\delta_Ra_R^{-1}$. Here $\theta_{f,R}$ is the orientation of [thm-pur-diagonal-dualizing-object], i.e. the diagonal construction, which that theorem forms over the preimages $X_i=f^{-1}(V_i)$ of an affine open cover $\{V_i\}$ of $Y$ and glues. In our separated setting the global composite $\beta_R\delta_Ra_R^{-1}$ is defined on all of $X$, and it restricts on each $X_i$ to the local composite for $f_i:X_i\to V_i$: the pair $(W,\Delta)$ and the normal bundle $N_\Delta$ restrict to $(X_i\times_{V_i}X_i,\Delta_i)$ and $N_{\Delta_i}$; $a_R$ restricts to the diagonal arrow of $f_i$ because the canonical comparison of the base-change clause of [thm-pur-cohomological-smoothness] is compatible with base change, here along the open immersion $X_i\hookrightarrow X$; $\delta_R$ restricts to the comparison for $(p_{1,i},\Delta_i)$ by the localization and base-change clause of [thm-pur-dnc-invariance]; and $\beta_R$ restricts to the zero-section arrow of $N_{\Delta_i}$ by the base-change compatibility of [cor-pur-vector-bundle-purity]. Both $\theta_{f,R}$ and $\beta_R\delta_Ra_R^{-1}$ are isomorphisms $\omega_{f,R}\to R_X(d)[2d]$; after removing the common shift $[2d]$ both source and target are sheaves in degree zero, so the two maps are sheaf maps by [lem-weil-pbc-derived-single-fully-faithful], and they agree on the cover $\{X_i\to X\}$, hence globally by [lem-pur-sheaf-hom-cover-gluing]. Thus $\theta_{f,R}=\beta_R\delta_Ra_R^{-1}$, independently of the cover. Substitute the three equations proved in Steps 2–3. They give
$$\theta_{f,A}^{\mathrm{dir}}c_f
=\beta_A\delta_Aq_{p_1,\Delta}(a_R)_A^{-1}
=(\beta_R)_A(\delta_R)_A(a_R)_A^{-1}
=(\theta_{f,R})_A.$$
Since $c_f$ is invertible, $\theta_{f,A}^{\mathrm{dir}}=(\theta_{f,R})_Ac_f^{-1}=\theta_{f,A}^{(n)}$. This proves clause (2).
